      {
        "code": "import numpy as np\n\ndef priority(item: float, bins: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Return one priority for each feasible bin.\n\n    ``bins`` contains remaining capacities after filtering bins that cannot\n    hold ``item``.  The evaluator selects the first maximum priority and\n    opens a new bin when the array is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Primary: prefer the tightest fit (smallest remaining space after placing item).\n    # Secondary: among equal tightness, prefer the bin with less absolute remaining capacity.\n    # This is equivalent to maximizing (-(bins - item)) + small * (-bins), but we use\n    # a direct formula that remains stable and numerically simple.\n    residual_after = bins - item\n    return -residual_after - 1e-6 * bins",
